WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:16.720
It was early one evening.

2
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.742
Principal Penn and the teachers were arriving at Metro City Grand Hotel.

3
00:00:24.004 --> 00:00:25.584
A mysterious man named Mr.

4
00:00:25.644 --> 00:00:27.726
Sweeps had invited them to a special meeting.

5
00:00:27.746 --> 00:00:33.336
"Maybe he's going to donate money to the school," thought Principal Penn.

6
00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:37.078
"Welcome," said Mr.

7
00:00:37.118 --> 00:00:39.498
Sweeps. "Please take a button."

8
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.921
Principal Penn pinned a star button onto her jacket.

9
00:00:48.702 --> 00:00:49.682
Then she sat down.

10
00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:52.063
"Now," said Mr.

11
00:00:52.103 --> 00:01:06.005
Sweeps. "Let me tell you why I invited you here It was a beautiful fall morning.

12
00:01:06.985 --> 00:01:08.846
Roxy and her friends were walking to school.

13
00:01:08.866 --> 00:01:12.487
"I hope the weather stays like this," said Jack.

14
00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:15.628
"Our class has a field trip to the zoo next week."

15
00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.870
"I can't wait to see the snakes," said Terrell.

16
00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.012
"I'm worried we won't be able to go to the zoo," said Mara.

17
00:01:24.032 --> 00:01:26.873
"My mom told me our school needs money.

18
00:01:27.793 --> 00:01:30.694
The field trip to the zoo might be canceled."

19
00:01:30.714 --> 00:01:33.276
"That would be awful!"

20
00:01:33.656 --> 00:01:34.176
said Jack.

21
00:01:35.484 --> 00:01:36.624
"We should do something to help."

22
00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:39.045
"What can we do?"

23
00:01:39.545 --> 00:01:40.145
asked Mara.

24
00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:42.226
"We don't have any money."

25
00:01:42.246 --> 00:01:45.987
"Maybe Rocket Girl can help," said Terrell.

26
00:01:46.007 --> 00:01:49.968
"I don't think so," said Roxy.

27
00:01:49.988 --> 00:01:52.409
"Rocket Girl doesn't have money."

28
00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:56.671
"Rocket Girl can do anything," said Terrell.

29
00:01:56.691 --> 00:01:59.651
"She's the greatest superhero ever!"

30
00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:01.192
Roxy shrugged.

31
00:02:03.824 --> 00:02:05.846
Soon Roxy and her friends reached school.

32
00:02:06.866 --> 00:02:08.167
Roxy looked at the parking lot.

33
00:02:08.187 --> 00:02:11.009
"Where are all the teachers' cars?"

34
00:02:11.309 --> 00:02:11.870
she wondered.

35
00:02:18.174 --> 00:02:21.416
students!" said a man at the school entrance.

36
00:02:23.277 --> 00:02:25.239
He was handing out star-shaped buttons.

37
00:02:25.259 --> 00:02:27.040
"I'm Mr.

38
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.362
Sweeps, your substitute principal today.

39
00:02:30.522 --> 00:02:34.584
Principal Penn is um busy doing other things."

40
00:02:36.265 --> 00:02:37.265
Roxy looked at Mr.

41
00:02:37.285 --> 00:02:38.345
Sweeps suspiciously.

42
00:02:39.406 --> 00:02:42.067
Something about the substitute principal seemed odd.

43
00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:44.847
"Cool! Thanks for the button!"

44
00:02:45.187 --> 00:02:45.748
said Jack.

45
00:02:47.308 --> 00:02:48.989
Mr. Sweeps handed one to Roxy.

46
00:02:49.009 --> 00:02:52.310
"Here you go, young lady," he said.

47
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.451
"Thanks," said Roxy, carefully looking at the button.

48
00:02:56.471 --> 00:02:59.912
"Go ahead, put it on," said Mr.

49
00:02:59.932 --> 00:03:03.794
Sweeps. Just then Roxy heard her watch beep.

50
00:03:04.795 --> 00:03:06.076
She put the button in her pocket.

51
00:03:07.157 --> 00:03:09.238
Then she hurried away from the school's entrance.

52
00:03:13.562 --> 00:03:15.143
Roxy pressed a button on her watch.

53
00:03:15.163 --> 00:03:19.767
"Mayor Bloom," she said.

54
00:03:19.787 --> 00:03:20.688
"What's wrong?"

55
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:24.491
"We have a problem, Rocket Girl," said the mayor.

56
00:03:24.511 --> 00:03:26.793
"Principal Penn disappeared.

57
00:03:27.794 --> 00:03:29.576
I want you to find out what happened to her."

58
00:03:30.696 --> 00:03:31.858
Roxy looked over at Mr.

59
00:03:31.898 --> 00:03:32.258
Sweeps.
